-- title:
--   Coefficient rigidity of the crossing presentation
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a nonzero $N$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $red : A \to k$; fix modular polynomial data for $q$ (a monic $\Phi \in \mathbb Z[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(q)$ annihilating the pair $(j, j_q)$) together with a Kronecker congruence for it, integrality of the Hecke $\bar\alpha$- and $\bar\beta$-homomorphisms for $(\overline{\mathbb Q}, N, q)$, a place specialisation $P$ for these data and a prolongation tuple $R$ over $P$. Let $K \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb Q$, $w$ a place of the modular function field $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC}\ k\ N$ over $k$, and let $O := A \cap K$ be the coefficient subring `NodeLocalized.coeffSubring A K`, assumed to be a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by an element $\varpi \in O$. Let $B := R.\mathtt{nodeIntegersOver}\ K\ w$ be the subring of elements of the field $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldBar}(Nq)$ that lie in $R.\mathtt{nodeIntegers}\ w$ and whose Laurent expansion lies in $\mathtt{NodeLocalized.fieldOver}(Nq)\,K$; $B$ is assumed local and Noetherian, and assumed to satisfy: for every $g \in B$ there is $o \in O$ with $g - R.\mathtt{nodeConst}\ K\ w\ o$ a non-unit, where $\mathtt{nodeConst}$ sends $o$ to the corresponding constant function. Let $W$ be a complete (for its maximal-ideal topology) discrete valuation domain, $\pi \in W$ irreducible, $E \ge 1$, and let $\iota$ be a ring isomorphism from the adic completion of $B$ at its maximal ideal onto $\mathtt{UVCrossingModel}\ W\ (\pi^E)$, the quotient of $W[[U,V]] = \mathtt{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\ 2)\ W$ by the ideal $\mathtt{uvCrossingIdeal}\ W\ (\pi^E)$, such that $\iota$ carries the image of $\mathtt{nodeConst}\ K\ w\ \varpi$ to $\mathrm{const}(\pi^E)\,\pi$, the class of the constant series $\pi$. The conclusion is that there exists a ring isomorphism $\tau$ from the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal onto $W$ such that, for every $o \in O$, $\iota$ carries the image of $\mathtt{nodeConst}\ K\ w\ o$ in the completion of $B$ to the constant class $\mathrm{const}(\pi^E)\,(\tau(\hat o))$, and $\tau(\hat\varpi) = \pi$.
--
--   This is the rigidity statement accompanying a crossing presentation of the completed node ring: once the completion of $B$ is identified with a two-variable crossing model over $W$ carrying the uniformiser $\varpi$ to $\pi$, the completed coefficient ring $\widehat O$ is identified with $W$ itself, compatibly with the inclusion of constants. It is used downstream in the computation of residues and of orders of vanishing of the two branch parameters at a supersingular node of $X_0(Nq)$.
